## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design a lightweight, beginner-friendly tracing path that minimizes overhead while providing end-to-end visibility across CNPA components.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight, opt-in tracing to avoid Always-On overhead
- Sampling strategies (1%) to bound performance impact
- Data minimization and PII redaction for compliance
- Asynchronous persistence to prevent blocking request handling
- Storage choice between Postgres (structured queries) vs Redis (high throughput, shorter retention)
- Observability integration and performance regression testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: activate trace if header is set, then persist asynchronously
function traceMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  if (req.headers['x-trace'] !== 'true') return next();

  const shouldSample = Math.random() < 0.01; // 1% sampling
  if (!shouldSample) return next();

  const traceData = {
    request_id: generateUUID(),
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    user_id: redactPii(req.user?.id), // PII redaction
    action: req.path,
    db_pointer: null
  };

  // Async persist - non-blocking
  persistTrace(traceData).catch(console.error);

  next();
}

async function persistTrace(data) {
  await db.query(
    'INSERT INTO traces (request_id, timestamp, user_id, action) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)',
    [data.request_id, data.timestamp, data.user_id, data.action]
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
End-to-end latency across CNPA helps catch cross-hop regressions. This question probes practical instrumentation, sampling, and validation strategies under load.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing across HTTP, DB, Kafka, Redis
- Trace propagation and sampling decisions
- Per-hop timings, end-to-end latency budgets, circuit breakers
- Idempotent sinks and retry/backoff strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// OpenTelemetry setup (illustrative)
const api = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const tracer = api.trace.getTracer('cnpa');
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http_request');
  req.headers['traceparent'] = span.context().traceId;
  next();
  span.end();
});
```

